cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the accompanying manuscript."
title: "Semantic-Guided Differentiable Hierarchical Temporal Graph Learning for Class-Imbalanced Log Anomaly Detection"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of SDHTG, a log anomaly detection model that learns
  strictly nested action-level and entity-level soft boundaries inside a
  pre-constructed outer sample, uses the resulting soft membership matrix for
  differentiable hierarchical aggregation and as cross-level edge weights of a
  heterogeneous temporal graph, and couples the boundary network to the detection
  objective. The repository contains the preprocessing pipeline, the model and
  losses, all baselines and ablations, the interpretation and efficiency studies,
  and the scripts that generate the paper's figures, tables and supplementary
  material.
authors:
